.TH MYSTRNCPY 3 "September 2026" "BSDSF24A012-OS-A01" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mystrncpy \- copy up to a specified number of characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mystrfunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mystrncpy(char *dest, const char *src, int n);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mystrncpy
copies at most
.I n
characters from
.I src
to
.IR dest .
If the source ends before
.IR n
characters, a null terminator is written. The destination must have enough
space for the requested characters and terminator when needed.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 if a pointer is NULL or
.I n
is negative.
